# Allowlist: the build context is only what a Dockerfile stage COPYs. The bot stage takes
# LICENSE, NOTICE and src/; migrate runs `COPY . .` and its deploy steps also need alembic.ini,
# migrations/ (whose env.py imports src.models), scripts/ and the uv files, which modal's
# uv_sync uploads. Anything else in a local checkout (.pixi/, agent configs) stays out.
*
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!src/
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!alembic.ini
!migrations/
!scripts/

# Local artifacts inside the allowed directories.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.coverage
**/.DS_Store
